\ Curry/compose closures over already-compiled bases, dispatched at runtime in an
\ interpreter-free AOT binary. `apply` calls a quotation parameter it cannot see
\ the body of, so each closure reaches the compiled dynamic-dispatch path; the
\ closure pushes its captured prefix and jumps to the compiled base.
apply: ( x q -- y ) [ call ] ;

\ curry: [ + ] is a compiled base; capturing 10 yields [ 10 + ], applied to 5 -> 15.
5 10 [ + ] curry apply .

\ compose: two compiled bases [ 1 + ] then [ 2 * ], applied to 6 -> (6+1)*2 = 14.
6 [ 1 + ] [ 2 * ] compose apply .

\ nested curry: 20 then 10 captured over [ + ] -> [ 10 20 + ], called -> 30.
10 20 [ + ] curry curry call .
